  "assessment": [
    "Native observer uses original pyroute2 TCA_STATS fields and fails on missing stats; impairment/filter/route operations unchanged. Summed backlog is used only as zero/nonzero gate because hierarchical stats overlap.",
    "Historical native snapshots independently expose backlog and qlen despite old derived backlog observer bug. Every final pair audited below has native backlog=qlen=0. This is retrospective validation, not proof that the former derived observer itself worked.",
    "Analyzer separates successful-workflow latency, all-attempt terminal times, failure/status counts, deadline overruns, release/dispatch delay, per-operator compute and queue. No request-level significance testing or pure-network residual estimate.",
    "Verifier checks exact phase/allocation set, candidate/model/thread/source/transfer hashes and bytes, reference output quality, deadline, stable drain and retained native queue captures.",
    "Report correctly distinguishes fixed edge replay from live sensors, raw-ready clock from decode/sensing, TCP-split relay controls, per-Pod FIFO, finite-window overload, fresh serving implementation from interrupted attempts, and low6/high40 input-distribution confounding."
  ],
  "minor_followups": [
    "Chart subplot title queue growth should name observed E2E trajectory unless separate queue evidence is shown.",
    "Verifier records protected-after changes without making them a pass/fail gate; final reviewer must inspect changes and report any observed differences."
  ],
  "completion_preconditions": [
    "Full33-phase/606-attempt run finishes and cleanup/restoration artifacts are available.",
    "Run verify_load.py after completion; inspect protected-after changes and actual failed-request/deadline ledger.",
    "Document observer-only hot-update timestamp/hash and retrospective native audit separately from original runtime gate."
  ],
